RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
January 26, 2009
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met on this date beginning at 6:00 p.m. in
Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Ms.
Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Spiker and
Mr. Valdez.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Dan White,
City Attorney.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.) Mr. Collins moved to approve Consent
Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Brown. Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the
governing body.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
JANUARY 12, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
JANUARY 20, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Collins moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Valdez.  Mr. Brown moved to divide the question to allow for a separate vote on a voucher
payable to Ameri-Tech HVAC Services, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Motion to divide the question
carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.  Mr. Brown declared a conflict of
interest (business interest) due to the voucher payable to Ameri-Tech HVAC Services, and
vacated Council Chambers.  Mr. Collins moved to approve the voucher payable to Ameri-Tech
HVAC Services ($1,606.37), electric heat repair, seconded by Mr. Pierson.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present in Council Chambers.  Following
announcement of the vote, Mr. Brown returned to Council Chambers.  Upon inquiry, Barb Dorr,
City Treasurer, reviewed information available for vouchers payable to:  Hardung Appraisals
($275.00), property appraisal required for CDBG grant funding; SESAC, Inc. ($873.00), annual
license involving copy-written music; West Group Payment Center ($902.30), Westlaw
cases/statutes for attorney’s office; Wyoming Workers Compensation ($1,704.74), Cheyenne
Housing Authority (payment remitted through the City by CHA) and Police volunteers workers
compensation.  Main motion to approve remaining vouchers carried.  Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body.
Mayor Kaysen opened a public hearing to receive comments and input on the proposed
sale of real property owned by the City of Cheyenne, described generally as all those portions of
Lots 2, 3 and 4, Block 553, Original City, Cheyenne, Laramie County, WY (located south of 9th
```

