### Page 5 of 5

```text
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-15-09 for furnishing ammunition for the Police Dept., from
Ultramax Ammunition of Rapid City, SD; Scottsdale Gun Club of Scottsdale, AZ; BVAC, Inc.
of Florence, MT, and Lawmen’s and Shooters’ Supply, Inc. of Vero Beach, FL.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried (total bid amount of $58,020.00).
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #M-10-09 for a contract between the City of Cheyenne and DC
Construction, for a 40' x 56' post frame building at Taco John’s Ice and Event Center -- referred
to Finance Committee.
ANNOUNCEMENTS/REPORTS/MOTIONS:
Announcement was made of the appointment of Jack R. Spiker to the Downtown
Development Authority Board, to be confirmed   February 9, 2009.
OTHER CITY BUSINESS:
John Fafoutakis commented on potential annexation areas with close proximity to
railroad tracks and safety issues, and safety hazards involving drivers operating vehicles without
adequately clearing snow from vehicles resulting in limited visibility.
Mr. Valdez and Ms. Broyles advised that billboards have been placed throughout the
community in conjunction with the anti-graffiti and vandalism program, and provided contact
information to report violations as well as to receive graffiti clean-up information.
Ms. Broyles announced a meeting will be held Feb. 18, 2009 at 6:30 p.m., Bain
Elementary School, to provide information to Sun Valley area residents on establishing a
neighborhood watch program, and provided a brief update on the Cheyenne Methamphetamine
Initiative program.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 6:28 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
February 6, 2009
